==English==
{{was wotd|2008|January|1}}

===Etymology===
Early 15th century, from {{der|en|la-lat|reiteratus}}, past participle of {{m|la|reiterare|t=to repeat}} from {{com|la|nocat=1|re-|t1=again|itero|alt2=iterare|t2=to repeat}} from {{m|la|iterum||again}}.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiːˈɪt.ə.ɹeɪt/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiˈɪtəɹeɪt/|/ɹiˈɪɾəɹeɪt/|a=US,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-reiterate.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹiːˈɪtəɹæɪt/|[ɹiːˈɪɾəɹæɪt]|a=AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-reiterate.ogg|a=Queensland}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To say or do (something) for a [[second]] time, such as for emphasis.
#: {{syn|en|repeat|Thesaurus:reiterate}}
#: {{ux|en|Let me '''reiterate''' my opinion.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=April 23, 2012|author=Angelique Chrisafis| title=François Hollande on top but far right scores record result in French election| url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/world/2012/apr/23/francois-hollande-french-election| passage=He said France clearly wanted to "close one page and open another". He '''reiterated''' his opposition to austerity alone as the only way out of Europe's crisis: "My final duty, and I know I'm being watched from beyond our borders, is to put Europe back on the path of growth and employment."|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261013072314/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2012/apr/23/francois-hollande-french-election|archivedate=13 October 2026}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|I|ii|passage=You never spoke what did become you less / Than this; which to '''reiterate''' were sin.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To say or do (something) [[repeatedly]].
#: {{syn|en|repeat}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=1|passage=That with '''reiterated''' crimes he might / Heap on himself damnation.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|rare}} To say (something) for a [[second]] time, but word it differently.
#: {{syn|en|rephrase}}
#: {{ux|en|Was I hard to understand? Sorry, I'll try to '''reiterate.''' }}

====Usage notes====
Although {{m|en|iterate}} and {{m|en|reiterate}} are similar, {{m|en|iterate}} indicates that the action is performed for each of a set of items, while {{m|en|reiterate}} indicates a more general repetition.

